Circle $O$ is located on the coordinate plane with center at $(2,3)$.  One endpoint of a diameter is at $(-1,-1)$.  What are the coordinates of the other endpoint of this diameter?  Express your answer as an ordered pair.

Put your final answer within \boxed{}.

\textbf{Solution:}

The center of the circle is $(2,3)$.  The radius of the circle is the distance from the center to the other endpoint of the diameter.  The distance from the center to the other endpoint of the diameter is $\sqrt{(2-(-1))^2+(3-(-1))^2}=\sqrt{9+16}=\sqrt{25}=5$.  Therefore, the radius of the circle is $5$.

The other endpoint of the diameter is $5$ units away from the center of the circle.  The other endpoint of the diameter is $5$ units to the right of the center of the circle.  The other endpoint of the diameter is $5$ units above the center of the circle.  The other endpoint of the diameter is $(2+5,3+5)=(7,8)$.

Therefore, the coordinates of the other endpoint of the diameter are $(7,8)$.

The answer is: $(7,8)$

