Therefore, $60^2+80^2=YZ^2.$
Thus, $YZ=100.$
Since $WX$ is perpendicular to $YZ,$ we have $WX^2+WZ^2=YZ^2.$
Therefore, $WX^2+x^2=100^2.$
Thus, $WX=100-x.$
Since $WX$ is perpendicular to $YZ,$ we have $WX\cdot YZ=XY\cdot XZ.$
Therefore, $(100-x)\cdot 100=60\cdot 80.$
